# Local dev overrides — copy to `.env.development.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
# Vite loads `.env.development.local` after `.env.development`, so anything here wins.

# Enables the "Try the demo" button in local dev, and is the password it logs in with.
#
# In production this is a build-time secret (a Docker ARG fed from `secrets.DEMO_PASSWORD`
# — see Dockerfile and .github/workflows/publish-docker-hub.yml), so it is never set in a
# committed env file. Locally it's just the password of a throwaway dev account.
#
# Setup, once per dev stack:
#   1. Create a pymix account literally named `demo` (the /create-test-user-dev skill, or
#      POST /user/create against the local pymix). It gets its own navidrome/beets/
#      filebrowser containers, which is what `VITE_DEMO_NAVIDROME_USER=demo` in
#      .env.development then points at.
#   2. Put that account's password here.
#
# Logging in with it makes the app treat the session as a demo session, so the demo
# banner and the padlocked Sync tabs become reviewable locally. Note this is only a
# *shape* match for production: the real `demo` is additionally blocked server-side by
# pymix's `require_uploader`, whereas a plain dev account is not — so uploads will
# actually succeed locally rather than surfacing the locked state.
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD=
